Solution:-

Intuition :-
Digit manipulation through modulo and division to reverse integers and calculate absolute difference

Approach :-
let long long rev=0
Proceed rev=10*rev+x%10 for(int x=n; x; x/=10)
subtract rev-=n & return its absolute value
Add a Python code; it is a while loop using divmod in the ierations.
Add C code
Add Java code

Complexity :-
Time complexity: O(log 10 n)
Space complexity: O(1)

Code :-
class Solution {
    public int mirrorDistance(int n) {
        int mirror = 0, temp = n;
        while (temp > 0) {
            mirror = mirror * 10 + temp % 10;
            temp /= 10;
        }
        return Math.abs(mirror - n);
    }
}
